他实际上真的跟所有这些女人发生过性关系，而且他把这些都记录在一本剪贴簿里。

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:47.519
You know, it's sociopathic, edging into psychopathic, but he, it feels like these women really, he really did, he was with all these women.
你知道的，这带有反社会倾向，甚至边缘性地接近精神病态，但感觉这些女人确实……他真的跟所有这些女人在一起过。

00:11:47.519 --> 00:11:50.559
So I wondered if you guys ever, if that was ever absurd.
所以我很好奇你们有没有想过，这会不会太荒谬了。

00:11:50.559 --> 00:11:55.399
I didn't prefer it when you realize he does not have a very high success rate and he's making a lot of it up.
我其实更喜欢当观众意识到他的成功率其实并没有那么高，而且很多都是他瞎编的时候。

00:11:55.399 --> 00:11:57.799
And even in this one, he could still be making a lot of it up.
甚至在这集里，他其实也可能是在瞎编很多内容。

00:11:57.799 --> 00:12:05.799
If this one has a flots that were too committing to the idea that he's really getting all of these women, but we were so enamored over the idea of the bracket.
如果这一集有些地方过于执着于他真的搞定了所有这些女性的设定，但我们当时太迷恋对阵表这个创意了。

00:12:05.799 --> 00:12:14.960
This was, again, this was another one where it was like, hey guys, if you do a bracket, if you do like a March Madness themed episode, we'll promote you a lot in March Madness.
这又是一次这样的情况：嘿伙计们，如果你搞一个对阵表，做一个以疯狂三月为主题的节目，我们在疯狂三月期间就会大力宣传你们。

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:23.039
And this was like, you joined at a weird time, Joe, because the writer's guild strike, you were probably just getting used to having this job on how Mitch Mother and the writer's guild strike hit.
而且当时你加入的时机很诡异，乔，因为正赶上编剧工会罢工，你可能刚习惯在《老爸老妈浪漫史》里做这份工作，编剧工会罢工就爆发了。

00:12:23.039 --> 00:12:26.039
And then three months of, everyone was freaked out.
然后是三个月的停工，所有人都吓坏了。

00:12:26.039 --> 00:12:27.840
We were like, is this, are we gonna get canceled?
我们在想，这节目会不会被砍？

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:29.799
Is this the show gonna come out of this?
这节目还能挺过这一关吗？

00:12:29.799 --> 00:12:32.759
They have three months to realize they don't need me.
他们有三个月的时间来意识到他们根本不需要我。

00:12:32.759 --> 00:12:33.641
get rid of me.
然后把我踢开。

00:12:33.641 --> 00:13:03.414
I don't know if you remember you we threw this my episode was coming up and I was like hey everyone we're going on strike on Friday and I was like and you guys threw together a story and and sent me off to write it and told me to get it in and just write something down get it in I don't want to get in trouble with the WGA but you got me basically you got me paid right before the strike started you got me my script fee which I always thought was the coolest solid thing.
我不知道你还记不记得，当时我的剧集快要播出了，然后我说，嘿大家，我们周五要罢工了，接着你们俩临时拼凑了一个故事，把我打发去写剧本，告诉我赶紧把它写出来交上去——我可不想惹上美国编剧工会的麻烦——但你基本上是在罢工开始前让我拿到了报酬，让我拿到了剧本稿酬，我一直觉得这是最够义气、最酷的举动。

00:13:03.414 --> 00:13:07.127
But then we, and that was like, I really, I charged it out.
但随后我们……我当时真的是拼了命把它写完。

00:13:07.127 --> 00:13:08.701
I was really proud of it.
我当时为它感到非常自豪。

00:13:08.701 --> 00:13:15.751
And then like three months later, we come back from the strike and you're like, yeah, yeah, we're starting over.
然后大概三个月后，我们罢工结束回来，你们却说，对，对，我们要从头开始。

00:13:15.751 --> 00:13:17.576
That was the favorite of you.
这就是你们的“好意”。

00:13:17.576 --> 00:13:19.842
We are starting with the blank page.
我们要从一张白纸重新开始。

00:13:19.842 --> 00:13:22.549
And I was like, okay, thank you, thank you.
然后我就想，好吧，谢谢，谢谢。

00:13:22.549 --> 00:13:23.493
That's awesome.
这太棒了。

00:13:23.493 --> 00:13:34.383
Joe, what did you, when you, when I mean, you went on to obviously you're running shows now, but like, what did you learn from how I met your mother from that writer's room?
乔，当你在……我的意思是，你后来显然自己也在负责制作节目了，但从《老爸老妈浪漫史》那个编剧室里，你学到了什么？

00:13:34.383 --> 00:13:36.963
What did you learn from Carter and Craig?
你从卡特和克雷格身上学到了什么？

00:13:36.963 --> 00:13:41.432
What were the things like the gems you took from your time on the show?
有哪些宝贵的经验是你从那段节目制作经历中汲取并带走的？

00:13:41.432 --> 00:13:42.565
I would always do.
我一直都在这么做。

00:13:42.565 --> 00:13:47.475
On Detroiters, we just did it the same way because that's the only way I knew.
在拍《底特律人》时，我们也是用同样的方式做的，因为那是我唯一知道的方法。

00:13:47.475 --> 00:13:52.951
I just loved the breaking of story, the way we broke the story, and the doing it table.
我就是喜欢梳理剧情的方式，我们梳理故事的方式，以及在剧本围读桌上的做法。

00:13:52.951 --> 00:13:55.469
Just the structure of how much a mother.
这就是《老爸老妈浪漫史》的结构。

00:13:55.469 --> 00:14:30.404
And I'd always have little Carter's and Craig's over my ear of Carter's shoulder was you love this you love this idea on Monday love it on Friday don't don't lose faith in it and Craig on the other shoulder is is this line as good as it can be is this line as good as it could be can we beat this can we beat this and to not fall in love with things and like it really was like I've always every single moment of every page has always had those kind of two people that we were that you've thought of us that way because Detroiters is a fucking great show.
而且我的耳边总是回响着小小的卡特和克雷格的声音：卡特在肩膀上说，你周一喜欢这个创意，周五也要喜欢它，不要对它失去信心；而克雷格在另一边肩膀上说，这句台词是最好的状态了吗？这句台词还能再好一点吗？我们能精益求精吗？我们能超越现在的版本吗？——并且不要对任何东西爱得太深。真的就像是，每一页剧本的每一个时刻，脑海里总是有这两个人，也许你们觉得我们把你们当成那种……小天使和小恶魔，或者两个小天使，或者管他妈的什么呢。

00:14:30.404 --> 00:14:39.719
All of you've been such cool stuff since I'm very proud that we're even like little angel and devil or angel and angel or whatever the fuck we were.
但有趣的是，作为泰德原型的卡特，反而是那个说“不要失去信心”的人。

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:44.320
But it's interesting how Carter who was the model for Ted was the one who was like don't lose faith.
对啊。

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:45.320
Yeah.
他是个好人。

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:46.320
He was a good one.
是的。

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:47.320
Yeah.
是的。

