Yeah.
而且，倒不一定是指卡特和克雷格教给我的所有那些具体的事情，每当我回想起《老爸老妈浪漫史》时，因为正如你所说，我当时正处于那种状态：好吧，你们在搞所有这些烧脑的东西、浪漫的东西。

00:14:48.320 --> 00:15:01.799
And not, not, not necessarily Carter and Craig, with all of the, all of the things you all taught me, but when I think about how much mother, because I was, as you said, I was in that gear of like, all right, you guys are doing all this brainy stuff, romantic stuff.
我当时只是靠在椅子上，在你们让我抛出点子的时候，顺便抛出几个笑话而已。

00:15:01.799 --> 00:15:05.960
I'm just kind of leaning back in my chair and pitching bits when you ask me to pitch bits.
而你们真的把整部剧撑了起来。

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:12.520
And that was me learning from Chuck Tatham and Dave Hemmingson, who had, Dave was so busy on his own stuff.
那是我是从查克·塔瑟姆和戴夫·海明森身上学到的，戴夫当时忙于他自己的事。

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:19.019
He couldn't wait for five o'clock to go write two movies and go home and watch three more and play tennis.
他等不及到五点钟就要去写两个剧本，然后再回家看三个电影，顺便打网球。

00:15:19.019 --> 00:15:23.679
You know, he just had an amazing, her Miami grandeur like time turner thing.
你知道的，他就像拥有某种神奇的、像时间机器一样的东西。

00:15:23.679 --> 00:15:25.274
Is he coming the next day?
他第二天还要来吗？

00:15:25.274 --> 00:15:32.754
And it would be the math wouldn't add up of what he had done from when he left every single morning, every single morning.
而且按常理根本无法解释他每天早上离开以后，每天早上到底完成了多少工作。

00:15:32.754 --> 00:15:40.480
And then check Tatum was the opposite of like five o'clock man, I'm gonna grab a martini and set my my hot tub with the cigar.
而查克·塔瑟姆则完全相反，属于那种“五点钟一到，我就要拿上一杯马提尼，叼着雪茄泡我的按摩浴缸”的人。

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:41.480
Good.
行了。

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:42.480
Adios.
再见。

